  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft #354. Exposes the existing canonical task/RACI projection through GET /event-operations/events/{eventId}/tasks/{activityId}, strict DTOs, OpenAPI/generated web types and a runtime-validated web client. No alternate task system or placeholder workspace UI.\n\n## Requirements and invariants\n\nTA-01\u201305 refine TR-01\u201308 and EO-023\u2013028/045/051/055: exact target and current session binding, task-scoped authority, opaque denied targets, strict nested data, explicit accountability attention, no-store and lossless safe-integer numeric transport. The client cannot choose actor or evaluation time. Existing lifecycle/transition contracts remain intact.\n\nThe unchanged applicable TLC/Alloy models were rechecked successfully before adapter implementation. Finite checking is not an unbounded proof.\n\n## Executed checks\n\n- Before implementation: new real HTTP contract failed with expected 200 / actual 404; 36 prior examples passed.\n- Final focused Stack/Hspec/real HTTP/PostgreSQL suite: 63 examples, zero failures, including two 100-case property checks and after-auth task session revocation.\n- Web client: 29/29 contract tests; focused ESLint and strict TypeScript checks passed using unchanged project compiler options.\n- Generated web declarations reproduced byte-identically. Runner guards/dependency ordering: 4/4. Repository quality, OpenAPI parsing, shell syntax, whitespace and 86 documentation links passed.\n- Full pinned formal suite: positive models pass, 20 expected negative controls, two SAT scenarios and 11 UNSAT assertions in documented scopes.\n\n## Known blocker \u2014 whole-web typecheck is NOT green\n\nnpm run typecheck:ui exits 2 because LoginPage imports missing markWebSignupCompleted and AppShell imports missing retryPendingFirstValueCompletion from onboardingProgress. All three files are byte-identical to the base commit, whose source contains those same missing exports. No onboarding code or global CI gate was changed. The focused diagnostic is not a replacement for the failed full gate.\n\n## Schema/security/rollback\n\nNo production SQL, schema, manifest, grants, provider flags or submodule pointer changes. HTTP runners install existing task migrations only in disposable databases. Roll back route/client consumers first; retain the read-only SQL helpers or use their existing function-only rollback once consumers stop. No domain/history deletion.\n\n## Remaining limitations\n\nCurrent-head full backend compilation/tests and remote CI are not verified. The inherited long-running no-run-tests build is still recompiling after source changes; it is not a completed stable-head test result. Mobile checkout is uninitialized; no mobile, browser/a11y, performance or payment sandbox claim. Global-role catalog revalidation, aggregate write tokens, membership removal and workspace views remain next.\n\nDraft only. Do not merge, deploy, activate credentials/providers or perform real-money operations.\n\n[Detailed evidence, exact commands and rollback](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/881882e15cd1b2400cc2e0452ea50683dea675de/docs/event-operations/pr-14-task-read-api.md)",
